1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,492
Ravi now runs two Chai Corners,
and Meena runs outlet two.

2
00:00:04,792 --> 00:00:07,776
But every morning, Ravi
just hands her a new order.

3
00:00:08,326 --> 00:00:09,730
Monday, sell more.

4
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:11,183
Tuesday, save milk.

5
00:00:11,183 --> 00:00:12,882
Wednesday, open earlier.

6
00:00:13,182 --> 00:00:15,994
Meena never gets a say,
so she stops trying.

7
00:00:16,294 --> 00:00:19,414
And at the end of the month,
nobody knows if she did well.

8
00:00:20,064 --> 00:00:21,604
Orders are not enough.

9
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:24,346
Ravi and Meena need to set goals together.

10
00:00:25,046 --> 00:00:27,634
So, what is management by objectives?

11
00:00:27,934 --> 00:00:33,316
In 1954, Peter Drucker made the idea
famous in his book, The Practice of

12
00:00:33,316 --> 00:00:34,302
Management.

13
00:00:34,652 --> 00:00:39,395
MBO means the manager and the worker
agree on clear goals together, then

14
00:00:39,395 --> 00:00:41,605
judge the work by its results.

15
00:00:42,205 --> 00:00:44,227
So Ravi stops giving orders.

16
00:00:44,227 --> 00:00:47,276
He and Meena sit down
and agree on targets.

17
00:00:47,926 --> 00:00:49,903
MBO runs in five steps.

18
00:00:50,353 --> 00:00:51,253
One.

19
00:00:50,893 --> 00:00:53,160
Set the organization's objectives.

20
00:00:53,160 --> 00:00:58,499
Remember Ravi's SMART goal: five hundred
cups a day at outlet two, by March.

21
00:00:58,849 --> 00:00:59,749
Two.

22
00:00:59,391 --> 00:01:01,931
Set individual objectives, together.

23
00:01:01,931 --> 00:01:07,063
Meena suggests her own target: two
hundred cups before ten in the morning.

24
00:01:07,063 --> 00:01:08,094
Ravi agrees.

25
00:01:08,444 --> 00:01:09,344
Three.

26
00:01:09,078 --> 00:01:10,461
Make action plans.

27
00:01:10,461 --> 00:01:15,170
Meena decides how: an extra helper
at seven, and cups washed the night

28
00:01:15,170 --> 00:01:16,070
before.

29
00:01:16,207 --> 00:01:17,107
Four.

30
00:01:16,758 --> 00:01:17,909
Review progress.

31
00:01:17,909 --> 00:01:22,445
Every Friday, they check the numbers
together, and fix problems early.

32
00:01:22,795 --> 00:01:23,695
Five.

33
00:01:23,342 --> 00:01:24,738
Appraise and reward.

34
00:01:24,738 --> 00:01:29,465
By March, Meena hits two hundred,
and she earns a bonus for the result.

35
00:01:30,115 --> 00:01:32,191
Why does MBO work so well?

36
00:01:32,540 --> 00:01:33,440
Clarity.

37
00:01:33,305 --> 00:01:35,622
Meena knows exactly what counts.

38
00:01:35,972 --> 00:01:36,872
Motivation.

39
00:01:36,748 --> 00:01:39,638
She chose the target,
so she wants to hit it.

40
00:01:39,989 --> 00:01:41,361
And participation.

41
00:01:41,361 --> 00:01:43,478
The worker gets a real say.

42
00:01:44,128 --> 00:01:45,987
But MBO has limits too.

43
00:01:46,337 --> 00:01:47,499
It takes time.

44
00:01:47,499 --> 00:01:50,975
Setting goals and reviewing
them means many meetings.

45
00:01:51,325 --> 00:01:53,627
And it can focus too much on numbers.

46
00:01:53,627 --> 00:01:56,848
Chase only cups, and the
taste of the chai may slip.

47
00:01:57,498 --> 00:01:58,467
Quick check.

48
00:01:58,467 --> 00:02:02,365
Ravi writes Meena's targets
alone, and just hands them over.

49
00:02:02,365 --> 00:02:04,423
Which part of MBO is missing?

50
00:02:06,323 --> 00:02:07,407
Participation!

51
00:02:07,407 --> 00:02:11,323
In MBO, the manager and the
worker set goals together.

52
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:12,932
So, remember.

53
00:02:13,232 --> 00:02:18,157
MBO means setting clear, measurable
goals together, and judging by results.

54
00:02:18,507 --> 00:02:23,497
It runs in five steps: objectives,
individual goals, action plans, review,

55
00:02:23,497 --> 00:02:24,432
and reward.

56
00:02:24,782 --> 00:02:28,926
It brings clarity and motivation,
but watch the time and the numbers.

57
00:02:29,526 --> 00:02:34,674
Next time, Ravi faces a big choice,
and learns the decision-making process.
